## 4. NVIDIA Corporation (NVDA)

### Company Overview

NVIDIA Corporation is a leading semiconductor and computing company. It is best known for its graphics processing units (GPUs), which have become essential for artificial intelligence, machine learning and data-center applications.

The company has become one of the biggest beneficiaries of the global AI boom.

### Key Indicators

| Indicator             | Details                |
| --------------------- | ---------------------- |
| Company               | NVIDIA Corporation     |
| Ticker Symbol         | NVDA                   |
| Exchange              | NASDAQ                 |
| Share Price           | Approximately $220     |
| Market Capitalization | Above $5 Trillion      |
| Main Growth Areas     | AI Chips, Data Centers |

### Price Trend

NVIDIA has experienced exceptional growth over recent years because of increasing demand for AI computing infrastructure. Its stock has also been considerably more volatile than many mature technology companies.

The strong demand for NVIDIA's GPUs has made the company a critical supplier to major technology and cloud companies.

### Recent News and Performance

NVIDIA's latest financial results demonstrated continued strength in its AI and data-center businesses. Recent reports highlighted quarterly revenue of approximately **$96 billion**, with data-center revenue around **$89 billion**. The company also provided strong forward guidance of approximately **$108 billion** for the following quarter.

These results demonstrate the continuing demand for AI infrastructure.

**Strengths:**

* Leading position in AI GPUs
* Very strong data-center growth
* High demand for AI infrastructure
* Strong revenue and earnings growth
* Large AI software ecosystem

**Risks:**

* High market expectations
* High stock-price volatility
* Semiconductor competition
* Geopolitical restrictions
* Dependence on continued AI investment

